873 0 obj
<<
/Title (Environmental PAH exposure is associated with epigenetic age acceleration, while mechanistic evidence supports DNA adduct formation, oxidative stress,  inflammation, and abnormal DNAm as intermediate processes. These biological changes are correlated with weakened DNA repair, disrupted tumor-suppressor pathways, and increased genomic instability, creating conditions that support lung carcinogenesis. Human studies have associated PAH exposure with epigenetic age acceleration, while prospective studies have associated accelerated epigenetic aging, particularly GrimAge acceleration, with greater lung cancer risk. Although direct causality has not yet been proven, epigenetic aging is a promising risk biomarker and potential contributor to PAH-associated lung cancer risk.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 495 0 R
>>
endobj
