946 0 obj
<<
/Title (Polycyclic Aromatic Hydrocarbons \(PAHs\) are a class of organic compounds composed of two or more fused aromatic rings [24]. Humans are exposed to PAHs through occupational sources of coke-oven work [9,10,20], coal mining [22], and chimney sweeping [25,27,31], or through everyday sources like vehicle emissions [6,12], tobacco smoke [5,16], and charred meats [2]. PAHs can be metabolized into reactive intermediates that bind to DNA and cause mutations [1,17,24] or indirectly trigger oxidative stress and inflammation [2,22,28]. DNA methylation \(DNAm\) is an epigenetic modification in which a methyl group is primarily attached to the cytosine residue within a cytosine-guanine \(CpG\) site [18,27]. DNAm patterns can be used to calculate epigenetic age, an estimate of biological aging relative to chronological age [7,9,16]. Few studies have examined the full pathway linking PAH exposure, epigenetic age acceleration, and DNAm alterations with lung carcinogenesis [7,23,29,32].)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 871 0 R
>>
endobj
